=== P2 Shared surface 0050 AIStateMachineDebuggerNarrator (Windows) ===

Surface: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/AIStateMachineDebuggerNarrator.{Model,Source,ViewModel}.cs + .cs (view)
Tests:   apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/AIStateMachineDebuggerNarratorTests.cs
Web src: web/src/components/ai/AIStateMachineDebuggerNarrator.tsx (THE specification)

Parity port of the web AIStateMachineDebuggerNarrator composed with its shared AIFeatureCard scaffold and the
withAiFeature gate. On-demand Helix narration of the deterministic per-vehicle FSM transition trace: the action
POSTs the in-scope { vehicle_id, from_unix, to_unix } body to /api/v1/ai/system/fsm/narrate via the canonical
useAiStream SSE contract and streams the narrative into the output region. The deterministic transition table /
state diagram / FSM health panel / timeline remain the canonical baseline (ADR-015 I3); this is the opt-in
narration section beneath them.

Architecture (mirrors the shipped AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative narrate-surface, the closest analogue — same
POST-body -> narrate-path -> SSE-stream shape). Each AI shared surface owns its own stream stack (AIDriveCoaching
uses AiCoach*, AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative uses AiNarration*); only IAiFeatureGate is shared. This surface
uses the FsmNarrate* prefix:
  - .Model.cs       : AIStateMachineDebuggerNarratorRegistration (FeatureId/Slug/RootAutomationId/NarratePath +
                      the five web i18n keys with catalog-verified fallbacks), FsmNarrateStreamState /
                      FsmNarrateEventKind / FsmNarrateErrorReason, FsmNarrateStreamEvent, FsmNarrateRequest
                      (vehicle_id/from_unix/to_unix, snake_case-pinned), FsmNarrateSseParser (native port of
                      useAiStream parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent), AIStateMachineDebuggerNarratorDiagnostics.
  - .Source.cs      : IFsmNarrateStreamTransport (P1/S8 seam) + HttpFsmNarrateStreamTransport (POSTs the body,
                      reads text/event-stream, classifies HTTP vs Network failure). Reuses the shared
                      IAiFeatureGate / StaticAiFeatureGate / DelegateAiFeatureGate (canonical home:
                      AICabinTemperatureImpactNarrative.Source.cs).
  - .ViewModel.cs   : UI-thread-free state holder. Gate (IsGateOpen), the haveScope guard
                      (CanStart = vehicle_id>0 AND from_unix>0 AND to_unix>from_unix), the emptyHint
                      (ShowEmptyHint = !CanStart), the useAiStream lifecycle (idle -> streaming -> done/error,
                      duplicate-start no-op, cancel -> idle), offline classification, and all projected labels.
                      No HTTP, no WinUI types.
  - .cs (view)      : WinUI 3 ContentControl. TsGlassPanel card -> header (PanelTitle + Helix TsBadge + Subhead
                      description + emptyHint Caption when !CanStart) + universal "Ask Helix" TsButton -> output
                      region (TsSkeleton thinking / Text narration / TsQueryError retryable, offline-aware error).
                      withAiFeature gate collapses the whole surface (Visibility.Collapsed + cleared automation id
                      + AccessibilityView.Raw) when the feature is off.

States rendered (on-demand SSE action — no cached prior result to age, so no "stale" state, matching the web
hook's stream_http_* -> error fallback): gate-off (collapsed) - idle with emptyHint - streaming/thinking skeleton
- accumulating narration text - error / offline (retryable QueryError). Every branch is asserted headlessly in
the view-model per-state tests (the headless snapshot of what the view renders in each state).

i18n: every string resolves through the ILocalizer facade (P1/S10). The five web keys
(stateMachineDebugger.aiNarrator.{title,description,button,badge,emptyHint}) plus the shared helix.* CTA keys are
present in apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json (verified); the registration fallbacks are the catalog values
verbatim. No English literals in the view.

Accessibility: Narrator name on the card and the badge; the action button carries the composed
"Ask Helix \u00b7 Narrate transitions" accessible name + the per-feature verb tooltip; decorative Helix glyph
marked AccessibilityView.Raw; thinking skeleton honours MotionPreference.ReduceMotion; streamed output uses a
LiveRegion so Narrator announces deltas.

Telemetry: AIStateMachineDebuggerNarratorDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=AIStateMachineDebuggerNarrator"
(PII-safe — never the narration text, vehicle id, or window bounds) once when the surface is shown (P1/S11).

Hook-URL verification (acceptance): NarratePath "/ai/system/fsm/narrate" matches the backend route
internal/api/ai_routes.go:510  r.Post("/system/fsm/narrate", g.Wrap("state-machine-debugger-narrator", ...))
(mounted under the /ai group, +/api/v1 prefix => /api/v1/ai/system/fsm/narrate). Feature id
"state-machine-debugger-narrator" is present in AiFeatureRegistry.Features (verified by test).

